# Embedded web builds — generated by server/build.sh, never committed.
#
# `go:embed` resolves at COMPILE time, so a missing dist/ or docs-dist/ is a
# compile error for the whole package (not just a broken binary): it would break
# `go build ./...`, `go vet`, `go test`, and gopls on a fresh clone. The tracked
# .gitkeep in each directory exists only to satisfy the embed pattern — `all:`
# matches dotfiles, and neither Vite nor Astro ever emits that name, so a real
# build adds no diff. spa.go / docs.go detect the stub and degrade gracefully.
dist/*
!dist/.gitkeep
docs-dist/*
!docs-dist/.gitkeep
